## MCP 1 — migration-fs

## Purpose: File system operations, Git operations, and migration state persistence

Build a complete MCP server exposing these tools:

### read_file

Input:  { path: string }
Action: Read file at absolute path (or relative to PROJECT_ROOT)
Output: { content: string, size_bytes: number, encoding: string }
Error:  { error: “FILE_NOT_FOUND” | “PERMISSION_DENIED” | “READ_ERROR”, detail: string }

### write_file

Input:  { path: string, content: string, create_dirs?: boolean }
Action: Write content to file. If create_dirs=true, create parent directories.
Output: { written: true, path: string, size_bytes: number }
Error:  { error: “WRITE_ERROR” | “PERMISSION_DENIED”, detail: string }

### list_directory

Input:  { path: string, recursive?: boolean, include_hidden?: boolean, extensions?: string[] }
Action: List files/directories. If extensions provided, filter by extension.
Output: { entries: Array<{ path: string, type: “file”|“dir”, size_bytes: number, extension: string }>, total: number }
Error:  { error: “DIR_NOT_FOUND” | “PERMISSION_DENIED”, detail: string }

### search_code

Input:  { pattern: string, glob?: string, case_sensitive?: boolean, max_results?: number }
Action: Search for regex pattern in files matching glob (default: **/*).
Use ripgrep (rg) if available, else grep.
Output: { matches: Array<{ file: string, line: number, content: string }>, total: number }
Error:  { error: “SEARCH_ERROR”, detail: string }

### get_state

Input:  {}
Action: Read migration_state.json from PROJECT_ROOT/.migration/state.json
Output: { state: object | null, exists: boolean, last_updated: string | null }
Error:  { error: “READ_ERROR”, detail: string }

### set_state

Input:  { state: object }
Action: Write state to PROJECT_ROOT/.migration/state.json (create dir if needed)
Always merge with existing state, never overwrite keys not provided
Append timestamp to state.last_updated
Output: { saved: true, path: string, last_updated: string }
Error:  { error: “WRITE_ERROR”, detail: string }

### get_git_log

Input:  { limit?: number, branch?: string }
Action: Run `git log --oneline -n {limit}` in PROJECT_ROOT
Output: { commits: Array<{ hash: string, message: string, date: string }> }
Error:  { error: “GIT_ERROR” | “NOT_A_REPO”, detail: string }

### get_git_diff

Input:  { base?: string, target?: string, file?: string }
Action: Run `git diff {base}..{target} -- {file}` or `git diff HEAD` if no args
Output: { diff: string, files_changed: string[], insertions: number, deletions: number }
Error:  { error: “GIT_ERROR”, detail: string }

### git_create_branch

Input:  { name: string, from?: string }
Action: Run `git checkout -b {name}` or `git checkout -b {name} {from}`
Output: { created: true, branch: string, from: string }
Error:  { error: “GIT_ERROR” | “BRANCH_EXISTS”, detail: string }

### git_commit

Input:  { message: string, files?: string[] }
Action: Run `git add {files or "."}` then `git commit -m "{message}"`
Output: { committed: true, hash: string, message: string }
Error:  { error: “GIT_ERROR” | “NOTHING_TO_COMMIT”, detail: string }

### git_current_branch

Input:  {}
Action: Run `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`
Output: { branch: string }
Error:  { error: “GIT_ERROR” | “NOT_A_REPO”, detail: string }

