## MCP 2 — migration-runner

## Purpose: Execute build, test, static analysis, and mutation testing

Build a complete MCP server exposing these tools:

### detect_project_type

Input:  { path?: string }
Action: Inspect PROJECT_ROOT for package.json, pom.xml, build.gradle,
Cargo.toml, requirements.txt, go.mod, *.csproj
Determine language and build tool.
Output: { language: string, build_tool: string, test_framework: string, confidence: “HIGH”|“MEDIUM”|“LOW” }
Error:  { error: “DETECTION_FAILED”, detail: string }

### run_command

Input:  { cmd: string, cwd?: string, timeout_ms?: number, env?: Record<string,string> }
Action: Execute shell command. cwd defaults to PROJECT_ROOT.
Capture stdout and stderr separately.
Enforce timeout (default 120000ms).
Output: {
exit_code: number,
stdout: string,
stderr: string,
duration_ms: number,
timed_out: boolean
}
Error:  { error: “EXEC_ERROR” | “TIMEOUT”, detail: string }

### run_build

Input:  { project_type?: string, args?: string[] }
Action: Auto-detect or use provided project_type.
Run the appropriate build command:
- npm/node → npm run build
- maven    → mvn compile -q
- gradle   → ./gradlew build
- cargo    → cargo build
- python   → python -m py_compile on all .py files
- go       → go build ./…
Parse output for errors.
Output: {
success: boolean,
project_type: string,
command_run: string,
errors: Array<{ file: string, line: number, message: string }>,
warnings: Array<{ file: string, line: number, message: string }>,
duration_ms: number,
raw_output: string
}

### run_tests

Input:  { project_type?: string, scope?: string, test_pattern?: string, args?: string[] }
Action: Run test suite for detected or specified project type:
- npm/node → npm test or jest –testPathPattern={scope}
- maven    → mvn test -Dtest={scope}
- gradle   → ./gradlew test
- cargo    → cargo test {scope}
- python   → pytest {scope} -v –tb=short
- go       → go test ./…
Parse results for pass/fail/skip counts.
Output: {
passed: number,
failed: number,
skipped: number,
total: number,
coverage_pct: number | null,
failures: Array<{ test: string, file: string, message: string }>,
duration_ms: number,
success: boolean,
raw_output: string
}

### run_static_check

Input:  { tool?: string, path?: string, config?: string }
Action: Run static analysis. Auto-detect tool if not specified:
- JS/TS    → eslint
- Python   → pylint or flake8
- Java     → checkstyle
- Go       → golint
- Rust     → clippy
Parse violations.
Output: {
violations: Array<{ file: string, line: number, rule: string, severity: “error”|“warning”, message: string }>,
error_count: number,
warning_count: number,
tool_used: string,
success: boolean
}

### run_mutation_test

Input:  { scope?: string, threshold?: number }
Action: Run mutation testing tool:
- JS/TS  → stryker (stryker run)
- Python → mutmut run
- Java   → pitest
threshold defaults to 80.
If tool not installed, return error TOOL_NOT_INSTALLED with install instructions.
Output: {
mutation_score: number,
mutations_total: number,
mutations_killed: number,
mutations_survived: number,
passed_threshold: boolean,
threshold: number,
survivors: Array<{ file: string, line: number, mutation: string }>,
tool_used: string
}

### get_test_baseline

Input:  {}
Action: Read .migration/test_baseline.json if exists
Output: { baseline: object | null, exists: boolean }

### save_test_baseline

Input:  { results: object }
Action: Write current test results to .migration/test_baseline.json
Output: { saved: true }

### compare_to_baseline

Input:  { current_results: object }
Action: Load baseline and compare to current_results.
Identify regressions (tests that previously passed now fail).
Output: {
regressions: Array<{ test: string, status: “was_passing_now_failing” }>,
improvements: Array<{ test: string, status: “was_failing_now_passing” }>,
regression_count: number,
is_regression: boolean
}

